{"author":{"id":"973fc03426eba9a243913e0f6e6823e102397744f60a9ab11c882af948c310c4"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1779637704,"nonce":"y4Lt4lYsivIwEh0KNkg9oVfP3po=","message":"## Additional evidence from Feedbax: reference-only issues closed by auth merges\n\nFeedbax now has a project meta coordination issue for cross-project/workflow concerns: Feedbax `1c01192`.\n\nDuring a Feedbax repo planning audit on 2026-05-24, three issues were found to have been closed by prior auth-request merges even though the auth request only satisfied part of the issue spec. They were reopened with comments documenting the remaining scope:\n\n- Feedbax `0c46f69` — Studio pipeline workspace spec. Merge `b682122b` delivered selector/metrics work, but the issue's pre-closure status explicitly said the broader pipeline workspace spec remained open.\n- Feedbax `85cec2c` — state browser panel. Merge `b682122b` delivered a curated selector picker, but not runtime/provider-backed PyTree schema browsing or validated selector lowering.\n- Feedbax `0258fac` — port constraints/type checking. Merge `27384a2` delivered a substantial schema/dimension/recurrence slice, but the issue still had open child/residual work around visual affordances, compatibility explanations, registry metadata, and closure/rescope decisions.\n\nThis is concrete evidence for the problem described here: auth requests need separate relationships for context references versus closure targets. Broad spec/coordination/umbrella issues often belong on the auth request for review and provenance, but they should not be closed unless explicitly listed as closing issues.","files":null}]}